                "text": "Here are the key Microsoft Learn entry points for the Azure OpenAI Service (OpenAI on Azure), plus commonly requested topics:\n\n- Azure OpenAI Service documentation (landing)\n  https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/ai-services/openai/\n- Overview\n  https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/ai-services/openai/overview\n- Quickstart guides (language tabs for Python, JavaScript, C#, Java, REST)\n  https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/ai-services/openai/quickstart\n- Models and availability\n  https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/ai-services/openai/concepts/models\n- Regions and availability\n  https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/ai-services/openai/concepts/regions\n- Quotas and limits\n  https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/ai-services/openai/quotas-limits\n- Content filtering and safety\n  https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/ai-services/openai/concepts/content-filter\n- Deploy and manage models\n  https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/ai-services/openai/how-to/deploy-models\n- Fine-tuning\n  https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/ai-services/openai/how-to/fine-tuning\n- Use your data (RAG with Azure OpenAI)\n  https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/ai-services/openai/concepts/use-your-data\n- REST API reference (Azure OpenAI)\n  https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/ai-services/openai/reference\n\nIf you want, tell me the specific topic (for example: “Python quickstart for GPT-4o,” “quotas in West Europe,” “fine-tuning GPT-4o mini,” or “content filter configuration”), and I’ll pull the most relevant Learn page(s) for that."
